-- title:
--   No equivariant map to a principal series at q when q² ‖ M
-- statement:
--   Fix $M \ge 1$ and a cusp form $g$ of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform in the sense of the project, i.e. a normalised eigenform such that no good eigensystem of $g$ occurs at a proper divisor of $M$. Let $\lambda$ be a prime, $S$ a finite set of primes, and $O'$ a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field in which $\lambda$ lies in the maximal ideal. Let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of the cusp forms generated by the Hecke generators away from $S$) to $\mathbb C$ sending each $T_\ell$, for $\ell$ prime with $\ell \nmid M$ and $\ell \notin S$, to the $\ell$-th $q$-expansion coefficient of $g$, let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from the range of $\chi_g$ into $O'$, and let $\rho$ be a [`GaloisRepAdic O'`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16): a free $O'$-module $V$ of rank $2$, finite over $O'$, with an adically continuous homomorphism from $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ (written as $\mathbb Q$-algebra automorphisms of $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$) to $\operatorname{End}_{O'} V$. Assume that for every prime $\ell \nmid M$ with $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $A$ (i.e. lies in the decomposition group and acts as $x \mapsto x^\ell$ on the residue field), the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \iota(\chi_g(T_\ell)) X + \ell$. Let $q$ be a prime with $q \neq \lambda$ and $\operatorname{ord}_q(M) = 2$, let $\Phi \neq 0$ be a function on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adeles of $\mathbb Q$ of which $g$ is an adelic lift (left invariance under the global points, right invariance under the finite level-one subgroup attached to the ideal $(M)$, and the prescribed value at matrices with trivial finite part in terms of the weight-two slash action of the archimedean part evaluated at $i$), and let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $P$, such that every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup at $P$ satisfying $\sigma(z)z^{-1} - 1 \in P.\mathrm{nonunits}$ for all $z \neq 0$ has $\rho(\sigma) = 1$. Let $j : O' \to O''$ be a ring homomorphism into a domain and let $a, b$ be functions from the Galois group to $(O'')^\times$ such that, for $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup at $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ maps under $j$ to $(X - a(\sigma))(X - b(\sigma))$, such that $a$ and $b$ are multiplicative on that inertia subgroup, such that $b(\sigma) = a(\sigma)^q$ and $a(\sigma) = b(\sigma)^q$ there, and such that $a(\tau)^{q-1} \neq 1$ for some inertia element $\tau$. Then for all characters $\mu_1, \mu_2 : \mathbb Q_q^\times \to \mathbb C^\times$, every $\mathbb C$-linear map $f$ from the adelic span of $\Phi$ to the carrier of the principal series attached to $(q, \mu_1, \mu_2)$ that satisfies $f(x \cdot v) = x \cdot f(v)$ for all $x \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_q)$ and all $v$ is zero.
--
--   This is the local statement at $q$ that the automorphic representation generated by the adelic lift of $g$ has no principal series quotient at $q$, under the hypothesis that the inertia labels $a, b$ at $q$ are interchanged by $q$-th powering and are regular ($a(\tau)^{q-1} \neq 1$); it strengthens the corresponding statement without the assumption $\operatorname{ord}_q(M) = 2$ by adding that hypothesis. It is used in the construction of a cuspidal local component of the prescribed type for the reduction of $\rho$, namely by [`CuspForm.IsNewform.exists_isCuspidalOfType_gl2ReductionRep_of_inertia_labels_eq_pow_of_irreducible_odd_of_cast_eq_neg_one`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsNewform.exists_isCuspidalOfType_gl2ReductionRep_of_inertia_labels_eq_pow_of_irreducible_odd_of_cast_eq_neg_one).
